shortname         = "self"
short_description = "develops this launcher itself"
full_description  = "Works on THIS project — the launcher's own repository (its Python packages, the agents/ tag tree, the tests, the docs). Bakes the launcher's dev toolchain into the image: the runtime deps its test suite imports (prompt_toolkit, python-dotenv, rich) plus mypy, so `bash check.sh` passes out of the box instead of failing on imports after every relaunch (ruff already arrives with [code]). Ships the project's own maintenance commands. Built on [code]; pointless for an instance whose workspace is any other project."
commands          = ["ai_project-test", "ai_project-update-models"]

[addendum]
title = "Developing the launcher"
body  = """Your workspace is the launcher project itself — the tool that built and launched you.

- **`bash check.sh` is the quality gate**: tests + lint + types, one definition, the same script CI runs. Run it before calling any change done.
- **The gate's whole toolchain is already available**: the runtime deps the test suite imports (prompt_toolkit, python-dotenv, rich) and mypy are baked into this image, ruff into [code]'s. Baked because installs made at runtime don't survive — containers are removed on exit and ~/.local is no mount — so image layers are the only place these tools persist.
- **`plans/ISSUES.md` is the live tracker** — problems that stay until fixed, each with its evidence and what would close it. Read it before re-investigating anything surprising; record new structural lessons there.
- **The `agents/` tree is validated at scan time** — a mis-shaped tag dir, dangling reference, or typo'd command name fails the test suite loudly via `scan_all`, so the gate covers tag-tree edits too."""
